{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"581f45644d92803ae8652802eb862b4a313c03ba3a4d2e7508d07c24e6dd4b6b","digest":{"component_or_area":"code-reading gates (review-plan)","key_entities":["rebar.llm.gate_source.resolve_gate_handle","rebar.signing._gate_commit_sha()","rebar._build_info.COMMIT","verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets","hatch_build.py"],"problem_keywords":["gate run","build drift","stale build","base ref","config mismatch"],"propositions":["A gate run does not detect when the running build's commit is a strict ancestor of the pinned base ref sha, allowing stale code to silently review current config.","Unknown config keys in a gate-pinned snapshot are reported as potential typos even when the running build predates the key rename, misdirecting operators to check documentation.","The drift detection must emit exactly one warning per (build sha, pinned sha) pair per process without failing the gate, altering the verdict, or changing provenance.","When the running build's commit is not present in the target repo or provenance is unavailable, the gate must remain silent and not attempt drift detection."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787408434828084001,"uuid":"dcd119d6-64b6-4d15-bec8-b3322f86394b"}